<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Prompt Engineering Guide</title>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Space+Grotesk:wght@300;400;500;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <style>
    * {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    body {
      font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
      background: #050816;
      color: #e5ecff;
      overflow-x: hidden;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .bg-grid {
      position: fixed;
      inset: 0;
      background-image:
        linear-gradient(rgba(255,255,255,0.03) 1px, transparent 1px),
        linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(255,255,255,0.03) 1px, transparent 1px);
      background-size: 40px 40px;
      z-index: -2;
    }

    .glow {
      position: fixed;
      width: 600px;
      height: 600px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(0,255,200,0.18), transparent 70%);
      top: -200px;
      right: -150px;
      z-index: -1;
      filter: blur(10px);
    }

    .glow-2 {
      position: fixed;
      width: 500px;
      height: 500px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(132,0,255,0.18), transparent 70%);
      bottom: -150px;
      left: -100px;
      z-index: -1;
      filter: blur(20px);
    }

    .container {
      width: min(1180px, 92%);
      margin: auto;
      padding-bottom: 100px;
    }

    .hero {
      min-height: 100vh;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      justify-content: center;
      gap: 24px;
      position: relative;
    }

    .badge {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 10px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.04);
      padding: 12px 18px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      width: fit-content;
      backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
      color: #9fffe7;
      letter-spacing: 1px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      font-size: 0.8rem;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6rem);
      line-height: 1;
      max-width: 900px;
      letter-spacing: -3px;
    }

    .gradient-text {
      background: linear-gradient(90deg, #8cf6ff, #8d7dff, #00ffbb);
      -webkit-background-clip: text;
      -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
    }

    .hero p {
      max-width: 760px;
      color: #b8c4e4;
      font-size: 1.15rem;
    }

    .hero-card {
      margin-top: 32px;
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
      gap: 20px;
    }

    .card {
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.05);
      border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);
      padding: 24px;
      border-radius: 24px;
      backdrop-filter: blur(14px);
      transition: 0.3s ease;
    }

    .card:hover {
      transform: translateY(-6px);
      border-color: rgba(0,255,200,0.4);
      box-shadow: 0 0 30px rgba(0,255,200,0.15);
    }

    .card h3 {
      margin-bottom: 10px;
      font-size: 1.1rem;
    }

    section {
      margin-top: 120px;
    }

    .section-title {
      font-size: 2.6rem;
      margin-bottom: 16px;
    }

    .section-subtitle {
      max-width: 760px;
      color: #b8c4e4;
      margin-bottom: 40px;
    }

    .grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr));
      gap: 24px;
    }

    .glass {
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.04);
      border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);
      border-radius: 28px;
      padding: 30px;
      backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
    }

    .glass h3 {
      margin-bottom: 18px;
      font-size: 1.35rem;
      color: #8cf6ff;
    }

    .glass ul {
      padding-left: 18px;
      color: #cbd7f5;
    }

    .glass li {
      margin-bottom: 10px;
    }

    .prompt-box {
      margin-top: 18px;
      background: #0b1025;
      border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);
      padding: 20px;
      border-radius: 20px;
      font-family: monospace;
      overflow-x: auto;
      color: #8dffcb;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
    }

    .timeline {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 22px;
    }

    .timeline-item {
      display: flex;
      gap: 20px;
      align-items: flex-start;
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.04);
      padding: 22px;
      border-radius: 22px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06);
    }

    .step {
      width: 44px;
      height: 44px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #00ffbb, #7b61ff);
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      font-weight: bold;
      color: #050816;
      flex-shrink: 0;
    }

    .timeline-item h4 {
      margin-bottom: 8px;
      font-size: 1.15rem;
    }

    .framework {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr));
      gap: 18px;
      margin-top: 30px;
    }

    .framework-card {
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.04);
      border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);
      border-radius: 20px;
      padding: 22px;
    }

    .framework-card h4 {
      margin-bottom: 10px;
      color: #00ffbb;
    }

    .footer {
      margin-top: 120px;
      text-align: center;
      padding: 60px 0;
      color: #8ea0c9;
      border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);
    }

    .highlight {
      color: #00ffbb;
      font-weight: 600;
    }

    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      .hero {
        padding-top: 100px;
      }

      h1 {
        letter-spacing: -1px;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="bg-grid"></div>
  <div class="glow"></div>
  <div class="glow-2"></div>

  <div class="container">
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="badge">AI • Systems Thinking • Creativity</div>
      <h1>
        Prompt Engineering <br>
        <span class="gradient-text">Built For Your Thinking Style</span>
      </h1>
      <p>
        Based on your conversation patterns, you naturally think like a founder, systems designer, and product strategist. You ask layered questions, connect industries together, and explore ideas deeply instead of seeking surface-level answers. This guide is designed around that mindset — practical, futuristic, strategic, and execution-focused.
      </p>

      <div class="hero-card">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>🧠 Your Prompt Style</h3>
          <p>You think in ecosystems, workflows, and scalable systems rather than isolated questions.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>🚀 Your Advantage</h3>
          <p>You naturally use iterative thinking — one of the strongest prompt engineering traits.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>⚡ Your Learning Path</h3>
          <p>Move from asking questions → designing AI workflows → building AI-powered businesses.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="section-title">What Is Prompt Engineering?</h2>
      <p class="section-subtitle">
        Prompt engineering is not just “asking AI questions.” It is the skill of structuring thinking clearly enough that AI becomes a strategic partner instead of a chatbot.
      </p>

      <div class="grid">
        <div class="glass">
          <h3>Beginner Level</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Ask better questions</li>
            <li>Get clearer outputs</li>
            <li>Use AI faster than others</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="glass">
          <h3>Intermediate Level</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Create reusable prompt systems</li>
            <li>Chain multiple prompts together</li>
            <li>Guide AI using frameworks</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="glass">
          <h3>Advanced Level</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Build AI workflows & agents</li>
            <li>Create AI-first startups</li>
            <li>Use AI as a thinking multiplier</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="section-title">The Founder Prompt Framework</h2>
      <p class="section-subtitle">
        This framework matches your natural way of exploring ideas.
      </p>

      <div class="framework">
        <div class="framework-card">
          <h4>1. Context</h4>
          <p>Explain the world, problem, or industry.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="framework-card">
          <h4>2. Objective</h4>
          <p>Define exactly what you want AI to achieve.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="framework-card">
          <h4>3. Constraints</h4>
          <p>Add limitations like budget, timeline, audience, or style.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="framework-card">
          <h4>4. Output Style</h4>
          <p>Tell AI how the answer should look.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="prompt-box">
You are a startup strategist.

Context:
I am building an AI workflow platform for MSMEs in India.

Objective:
Identify 5 operational pain points that can be automated using AI.

Constraints:
- Focus on companies with less than 100 employees
- Avoid expensive enterprise solutions
- Solutions should be deployable within 30 days

Output Style:
Use tables, practical examples, and implementation steps.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="section-title">Prompting Techniques You’ll Naturally Be Good At</h2>
      <div class="timeline">
        <div class="timeline-item">
          <div class="step">1</div>
          <div>
            <h4>Layered Prompting</h4>
            <p>You naturally ask follow-up questions. This is powerful because advanced prompting is iterative, not one-shot.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="timeline-item">
          <div class="step">2</div>
          <div>
            <h4>Systems Prompting</h4>
            <p>You think about workflows, ecosystems, and operations. That’s exactly how AI agents are designed.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="timeline-item">
          <div class="step">3</div>
          <div>
            <h4>Role-Based Prompting</h4>
            <p>You often explore perspectives like founder, builder, operator, investor, or customer. That improves AI depth dramatically.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="timeline-item">
          <div class="step">4</div>
          <div>
            <h4>Constraint Prompting</h4>
            <p>You frequently include practical limitations like budget, timing, market size, or scalability.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="section-title">Your Prompt Engineering Stack</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="glass">
          <h3>Research Prompts</h3>
          <div class="prompt-box">
Act like a market researcher.
Find hidden inefficiencies in the Indian construction supply chain.
Focus on problems that are frequent, expensive, and emotionally frustrating.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="glass">
          <h3>Startup Thinking Prompts</h3>
          <div class="prompt-box">
Pretend you are an early-stage VC.
Criticize this startup idea brutally.
Find weaknesses in scalability, distribution, and monetization.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="glass">
          <h3>Execution Prompts</h3>
          <div class="prompt-box">
Break this startup into a 30-day execution roadmap.
Focus only on MVP-level actions.
Avoid unnecessary complexity.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="glass">
          <h3>Creative Product Prompts</h3>
          <div class="prompt-box">
Generate futuristic product experiences for a smart home improvement brand.
Combine AI, retail, and consumer psychology.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="section-title">The 5-Level Evolution Path</h2>
      <div class="timeline">
        <div class="timeline-item">
          <div class="step">I</div>
          <div>
            <h4>Ask Better Questions</h4>
            <p>Most people stop here.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="timeline-item">
          <div class="step">II</div>
          <div>
            <h4>Build Repeatable Prompt Systems</h4>
            <p>Create reusable structures instead of random prompts.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="timeline-item">
          <div class="step">III</div>
          <div>
            <h4>Create AI Workflows</h4>
            <p>Connect research → strategy → execution → reporting.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="timeline-item">
          <div class="step">IV</div>
          <div>
            <h4>Build AI Agents</h4>
            <p>AI that thinks, acts, remembers, and automates tasks.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="timeline-item">
          <div class="step">V</div>
          <div>
            <h4>Create AI-Native Businesses</h4>
            <p>Where AI is part of the product, operations, and growth engine.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="section-title">Golden Rules For You</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="glass">
          <h3>Don’t Ask Small Questions</h3>
          <p>Your best prompts come when you explore systems, industries, and future possibilities.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="glass">
          <h3>Use AI Like A Thinking Partner</h3>
          <p>Debate ideas. Challenge assumptions. Stress-test concepts.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="glass">
          <h3>Iterate Aggressively</h3>
          <p>The first prompt is rarely the best prompt.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="glass">
          <h3>Design Prompt Architectures</h3>
          <p>Think beyond single prompts. Think workflows.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="section-title">Your Future Advantage</h2>
      <p class="section-subtitle">
        Most people use AI for answers. You naturally use it for exploration, systems thinking, and strategic ideation.
      </p>

      <div class="glass">
        <h3>Why This Matters</h3>
        <p>
          The future belongs to people who can combine:
          <span class="highlight">human creativity</span>,
          <span class="highlight">business understanding</span>,
          <span class="highlight">systems thinking</span>, and
          <span class="highlight">AI orchestration</span>.
        </p>
        <br>
        <p>
          Prompt engineering is not really about prompts.
          It is about structuring intelligence.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="footer">
      Designed around your thinking style • Futuristic • Strategic • Builder Mindset
    </div>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
